            "review_title": "Review at Ca Phe Do Phu - Com Tam Dai Han",
            "review_text": "Carsten G\nMelbourne, Australia39 contributions\n0\nLittle hidden Gem for its history\nAug 2019\nThis place should and must be preserved for its historical significance. \n\nIf you like stories of hiding in plain sight, trap doors, hidden tunnels, secret mailbox etc. Then this is well worth a stop. \nThis cafe was the secret base of operations. On the outside it was a restaurant. But behind the scenes it was a place for secret meetings, hiding place, secret mail box.\n \nIts a bit more off the beaten track, and I would suggest to make it a stop on a customized a guided tour, where the guide can show the trap doors and tell you the history of the place. \nDon't expect a Disney land where you crawl around in tunnels etc. There are no guide working there either. Its a working cafe which servers excellent coffee and a nice plate broken rice. \n\nThis is more a historical place and a hidden little gem for that reason.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten August 20, 2019",
